WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:04.219
The first optimization tool I'd like to talk about

2
00:00:04.219 --> 00:00:08.019
is the Unreal 5 console variables list.

3
00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:10.179
And to access this list, all you have to do

4
00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:13.820
is type the word help into the command prompt.

5
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.300
And Unreal will then, in your default web browser,

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.059
populate with a searchable file

7
00:00:22.059 --> 00:00:26.660
that allows you to look at each command Unreal Engine 5

8
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.660
offers, as well as provide a description of what

9
00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:32.340
that command does, and any parameters

10
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.060
it requires in order to work.

11
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.700
I highly suggest that everybody take

12
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.579
a look at this particular console variables help file.

13
00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:42.179
And again, to do this, all we need

14
00:00:42.179 --> 00:00:45.820
to do to get this to work is come to the Unreal Engine

15
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.820
editor, down to the console, type in the word help,

16
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.020
and press Enter.

17
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.500
Once we do that, our default browser of choice

18
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.619
will be loaded with this console variable system.

19
00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:02.659
We can then do things like adjust our render settings

20
00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:04.620
to just see the render options.

21
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.739
We can see all.

22
00:01:05.739 --> 00:01:07.700
But more importantly, like I said before,

23
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.819
this will give us the name of the command,

24
00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:12.500
and then a brief help description

25
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.739
of what that command does, as well as any parameters

26
00:01:15.739 --> 00:01:18.420
and what those parameters do.
